"""Render current research panels in their ordinary rank order."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,re
def rewrite_review(repo):
    repo=Path(repo);p=repo/'site/dist/review.html';text=p.read_text()
    evidence='https://github.com/sebastienpalcoux/grothendieck-ring-classification/tree/main/evidence/'
    audit=f'''<section class="review-panel" id="audit-correction"><h2>Audit and independent proof repair</h2><p>The old TPE completeness premise for R8_3_436 remains withdrawn. A separate spherical-equivariantization and formal-codegree proof now establishes its general exclusion. <a href="./case.html?id=R8_3_436">Read the replacement proof and exact certificate →</a></p></section>'''
    text=re.sub(r'<section class="review-panel" id="audit-correction">.*?</section>',lambda _:audit,text,count=1,flags=re.S)
    outcome='''<div class="review-panel" id="review-outcome"><h2>Current classification · 11 open questions</h2><p><a href="./unresolved.html">Open the current case directory →</a></p><details class="review-details" id="review-outcome-details"><summary>Classification counts and scope</summary><p>Rank nine through multiplicity two has 2,225 fusion rings: 2,145 general exclusions, 76 unitary models and four unresolved cases. Exact multiplicity two contributes 2,083 rings: 2,043 exclusions, 36 models and four unresolved.</p><p>Rank eight through multiplicity three has 4,403 general exclusions, 93 models and four unresolved cases. Its exact-multiplicity-three band has 3,507 exclusions, 16 models and four unresolved.</p><p>The other open cases are R6_4_155, R6_8_1660 and R10_1_189. Rank seven is classified through multiplicity five, and rank eleven at multiplicity one has 155 exclusions and 27 models. Completeness and verification retain their explicitly stated scopes.</p></details></div>'''
    text=re.sub(r'<div class="review-panel" id="review-outcome">.*?</div>',lambda _:outcome,text,count=1,flags=re.S)
    eight=f'''<section id="rank-eight-m3"><details class="review-details"><summary>Rank eight · current results and research history</summary><h3>Rank eight · multiplicity three</h3><p>The 3,527 exact-multiplicity-three rings have 3,507 general exclusions, 16 unitary models and four unresolved cases: <a href="./case.html?id=R8_3_928">R8_3_928</a>, <a href="./case.html?id=R8_3_941">R8_3_941</a>, <a href="./case.html?id=R8_3_1154">R8_3_1154</a> and <a href="./case.html?id=R8_3_1768">R8_3_1768</a>.</p><p>These four admit sphericality and Galois pseudo-unitarity reductions and have no braided Morita representative. Their necessary center data do not establish categorifiability. R8_3_436 is separately excluded by its new spherical-equivariantization proof; the old TPE parameterization remains withdrawn.</p><p><a href="./papers/rank8.pdf">Current manuscript</a> · <a href="./downloads/remaining_cases.py" download>Rank-six/eight open tensors</a> · <a href="{evidence}research_20261024">Proof repair and reconciliation</a> · <a href="./data/rank8_m3_attempts.json">Current attempt records</a></p></details></section>'''
    text=re.sub(r'<section id="rank-eight-m3">.*?</section>',lambda _:eight,text,count=1,flags=re.S)
    nine=f'''<section id="rank-nine-m2"><details class="review-details"><summary>Rank nine · multiplicity two</summary><h3>Rank nine · multiplicity two</h3><p>All 2,083 supplied tensors have source-bound decisions: 2,043 general exclusions, 36 unitary models and four unresolved rings. Ten exclusions and four coherent constructions settle fourteen cases from the earlier publication.</p><p>The remaining cases are R9_2_137, R9_2_1607, R9_2_1975 and R9_2_1976. All have no braided categorification. General existence reduces to pseudo-unitary existence after the audited sphericalization/Galois step; this does not make every original category pseudo-unitary or unitary. The three commutative sources reduce to two common necessary D8 Morita types; compatible associators and inverse modules remain unknown.</p><p><a href="./papers/rank9-m2.pdf">Current manuscript</a> · <a href="./unresolved.html?rank=9&amp;m=2">Four open cases</a> · <a href="{evidence}rank9_m2_20261024">Proofs, audits and exact replay</a></p></details></section>'''
    text=re.sub(r'<section id="rank-nine-m2">.*?</section>',lambda _:nine,text,count=1,flags=re.S)
    text=text.replace('All 26 open fusion tensors','All 11 open fusion tensors')
    from unresolved_retry_20261024 import active as retry_active
    if retry_active(repo):
        text=text.replace('11 open questions','10 open questions').replace('All 11 open fusion tensors','All 10 open fusion tensors')
        text=text.replace('The other open cases are R6_4_155, R6_8_1660 and R10_1_189.','The other open cases are R6_4_155 and R6_8_1660. Rank ten is complete at multiplicity one, with 136 general exclusions and 58 unitary models. R10_1_189 is recognized inside a classical conformal-embedding module category.')
        text=text.replace('The three commutative sources reduce to two common necessary D8 Morita types; compatible associators and inverse modules remain unknown.','The necessary D8 Morita rings have three types in their union. New stabilizer and Clifford theorems sharpen their cubic spectra; compatible associators and inverse modules remain unknown.')
        text=re.sub(r'(<section id="rank-ten-m1">).*?(</section>)',lambda m:m[1]+'<details class="review-details"><summary>Rank ten · multiplicity one complete</summary><p>All 194 rings are decided: 136 general exclusions and 58 unitary models. R10_1_189 is the charge-zero module subcategory from SU(4)_6 inside SU(10)_1; all 1,000 tensor coefficients match. This recognizes a classical construction.</p><p><a href="./case.html?id=R10_1_189">Model and proof</a> · <a href="./papers/rank9-rank10-m1.pdf">Current manuscript</a></p></details>'+m[2],text,count=1,flags=re.S)
        text=text.replace('Their necessary center data do not establish categorifiability.','Their necessary center data do not establish categorifiability. R928 has categorical Morita rigidity. For R1768 an actual twisted GH(C6,2) precursor now exists, but the required algebra 1+sigma remains unproved.')
    p.write_text(text)
